From: Kreijstal <elektrischrainbow@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 05:10:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ardour/test: fix the MinGW CPPUNIT_ASSERT_DOUBLES_EQUAL
 replacement

dsp_load_calculator_test.cc replaces CPPUNIT_ASSERT_DOUBLES_EQUAL on
MinGW (to avoid cppunit's "%.*g" string comparison) with a check that
rint(A/P) == rint(B/P). That is not the same as |A - B| <= P: two
values a hair apart on either side of a rounding boundary fail it,
which is what happens to the 48k/96k LPF comparison on Windows:

  equality assertion failed
  - Expected: 990
  - Actual  : 991

Compare the absolute difference against the tolerance instead, which
is what the original cppunit macro means and still avoids the string
formatting.
---
 libs/ardour/test/dsp_load_calculator_test.cc | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libs/ardour/test/dsp_load_calculator_test.cc b/libs/ardour/test/dsp_load_calculator_test.cc
index 6b774e5..37a0ac0 100644
--- a/libs/ardour/test/dsp_load_calculator_test.cc
+++ b/libs/ardour/test/dsp_load_calculator_test.cc
@@ -20,7 +20,11 @@ CPPUNIT_TEST_SUITE_REGISTRATION (DSPLoadCalculatorTest);
  * and this needs to go to https://sourceforge.net/p/cppunit/bugs/
  */
 #include <math.h>
-#define CPPUNIT_ASSERT_DOUBLES_EQUAL(A,B,P) CPPUNIT_ASSERT_EQUAL((float)rint ((A) / (P)),(float)rint ((B) / (P)))
+/* Rounding both values to multiples of P and comparing those is stricter
+ * than |A - B| <= P (values on either side of a rounding boundary differ
+ * by one step), so compare the difference directly.
+ */
+#define CPPUNIT_ASSERT_DOUBLES_EQUAL(A,B,P) CPPUNIT_ASSERT (fabs ((double)(A) - (double)(B)) <= (P))
 #endif
 
 using namespace std;
